│ patch_description        │ Replace the per-item linear scan over every pack with a min-heap of eligible packs. The   │
│                          │ previous implementation performs O(num_groups * num_packs) Python comparisons per layer,  │
│                          │ and repeatedly mixes Python integers with zero-dimensional Torch tensors. The heap        │
│                          │ implementation preserves the same greedy largest-processing-time assignment policy and    │
│                          │ capacity constraint, including deterministic pack-index tie breaking, while reducing      │
│                          │ assignment selection to O(log(num_packs)). It also materializes each layer’s weights as   │
│                          │ Python floats once, avoiding expensive scalar tensor operations in the inner loop. This   │
│                          │ reduces rearrangement latency without changing the placement heuristic or its             │
│                          │ load-balancing behavior.                                                                  │
