│ patch_name               │ vectorize_balanced_packing                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the nested Python loop over layers and groups in `balanced_packing` with a        │
│                          │ batched greedy packing loop. The original algorithm independently performs the same       │
│                          │ greedy choice for every layer, but executes tensor indexing, Python `min`, generator      │
│                          │ construction, and scalar updates once per `(layer, group)` pair.                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement keeps the same descending-weight greedy policy and exact per-pack         │
│                          │ capacity constraint, while processing all layers simultaneously at each sorted-group      │
│                          │ position. This substantially reduces Python overhead, avoids CPU scalar/tensor            │
│                          │ synchronization, and allows PyTorch to efficiently execute the per-layer pack selection   │
│                          │ and updates. Better algorithm execution time directly improves the speed component        │
│                          │ without changing the placement policy or its load-balancing semantics.                    │
