│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ vectorize_balanced_packing                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the per-layer Python greedy packing loop with a batched tensor implementation.    │
│                          │ The packing policy remains cardinality-constrained LPT: experts/groups are considered in  │
│                          │ descending load order and assigned to the currently least-loaded non-full pack.           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The original implementation performs Python loops over both layers and groups, repeatedly │
│                          │ converts tensor scalars through Python list operations, and is particularly costly when   │
│                          │ balancing many MoE layers. The new implementation retains only the unavoidable sequential │
│                          │ loop over sorted item positions; all layers select and update packs simultaneously using  │
│                          │ vectorized PyTorch operations. This substantially reduces rearrangement latency while     │
│                          │ preserving the same balancing heuristic and exact per-pack capacity constraint.           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0149                                                                                   │
