│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ heap_refined_eplb                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ This version improves the expensive balanced-packing stage while retaining the original   │
│                          │ public API and output formats.                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Replaces per-item tensor scalar operations and repeated Python linear scans with a      │
│                          │ heap-based least-loaded-pack assignment. This reduces pack selection from O(num_packs)    │
│                          │ per item to O(log(num_packs)).                                                            │
│                          │ - Processes each layer using Python-native numeric lists after a vectorized Torch sort,   │
│                          │ avoiding costly repeated CPU tensor indexing.                                             │
│                          │ - Adds a bounded local swap refinement after greedy packing. The refinement preserves the │
│                          │ exact number of items in every pack while reducing maximum pack load and load range when  │
│                          │ beneficial.                                                                               │
│                          │ - Keeps replication allocation vectorized in Torch, preserving the original greedy        │
│                          │ replica policy that minimizes the largest logical-expert load per replica.                │
│                          │ - Preserves hierarchical/global fallback behavior, tensor shapes, dtypes, mappings, and   │
│                          │ output semantics.                                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The local refinement is intentionally bounded, providing better GPU/node packing balance  │
│                          │ without making the algorithm expensive enough to outweigh inference-time gains.           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
│ api_costs                │ $0.0647                                                                                   │
