│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ fast_refined_packing                                                                      │
│ patch_description        │ Replace scalar PyTorch operations in `balanced_packing` with CPU-native Python data       │
│                          │ structures after the required CPU transfer. The previous implementation repeatedly        │
│                          │ indexed and assigned individual tensor scalars inside nested Python loops, which incurs   │
│                          │ substantial dispatcher overhead.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement uses a heap to select the least-loaded non-full pack in O(log(num_packs)) │
│                          │ time, rather than scanning every pack for every item. It also adds a bounded two-pass     │
│                          │ local swap refinement for small packing problems. This preserves exact pack cardinality   │
│                          │ while reducing pairwise load differences when the greedy assignment has a beneficial      │
│                          │ exchange available. The refinement is intentionally capped at 64 items, covering common   │
│                          │ expert/GPU layouts without making large configurations quadratic.                         │
│ num_applied              │ 2                                                                                         │
