│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ swap_refine_packing                                                                       │
│ patch_description        │ Add a small vectorized local-search refinement after cardinality-constrained LPT packing. │
│                          │ LPT is fast but can leave the currently heaviest and lightest GPU packs with a poor pair  │
│                          │ of expert assignments. Each refinement pass finds, per layer, the best legal swap between │
│                          │ those two packs that reduces their load gap while preserving the exact number of experts  │
│                          │ per pack.                                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The refinement is bounded to four passes, uses batched tensor operations instead of       │
│                          │ Python-level loops, and only accepts strictly improving swaps. It therefore improves the  │
│                          │ GPU maximum-load objective without changing expert replication counts, topology           │
│                          │ constraints, or output format. Since only the highest/lowest pair is examined each pass,  │
│                          │ it avoids expensive general NP-hard partition search.                                     │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
