│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ dual_waterfill_exchange                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This implementation uses two complementary optimization stages:                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Discrete dual water-filling for replicas**: replica counts are selected from the     │
│                          │ exact marginal sequence `load / replica_count`, which minimizes the largest per-replica   │
│                          │ expert load under a fixed physical-expert budget. A batched top-k path avoids sequential  │
│                          │ Python scheduling for normal model sizes.                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Vectorized cardinality-constrained LPT packing plus exchange refinement**: physical  │
│                          │ experts and expert groups are first assigned with batched least-loaded-pack scheduling. A │
│                          │ bounded all-pack-pair exchange pass then evaluates load-improving swaps between bins      │
│                          │ while preserving the exact number of experts per node/GPU. This improves difficult cases  │
│                          │ where greedy placement leaves complementary heavy/light experts on the wrong devices.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The algorithm remains hierarchical to preserve node-local expert groups, but removes the  │
│                          │ Python heap/list packing path and uses tensorized operations for substantially lower      │
│                          │ algorithm overhead.                                                                       │
