│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ vectorized_eplb                                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ This rewrite keeps the same EPLB API and output layout while reducing planner overhead in │
│                          │ the replica-allocation stage.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Uses a vectorized water-filling equivalent for replica counts when the candidate tensor │
│                          │ is reasonably sized. Selecting the largest `weight / replica_rank` marginal loads         │
│                          │ produces the same minimax replica allocation objective as iterative greedy water filling. │
│                          │ - Retains an iterative fallback for unusually large replica budgets to avoid excessive    │
│                          │ temporary memory.                                                                         │
│                          │ - Keeps cardinality-constrained LPT packing as the default GPU/node packer. It is         │
│                          │ deterministic, inexpensive, and avoids expensive quadratic swap refinement that has not   │
│                          │ shown measurable balance improvements in the supplied benchmarks.                         │
│                          │ - Reuses small helper functions for inverse permutations and logical-to-physical map      │
│                          │ construction.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The result preserves the physical-to-logical map, padded logical-to-physical map, and     │
│                          │ logical replica counts expected by callers.                                               │
